# What is versioned here is the composition and the reasoning behind it — the
# scene HTML, the plan layer (BRIEF / STORYBOARD / SCRIPT / frame), and the
# project config. Those are ~1 MB of text and are the actual work.
#
# Everything below is output or fetched media: ~75 MB that git would carry
# forever. Each entry says how to get it back, because "regenerable" is only
# true if someone knows the command.

# Rendered MP4s. Six of them, one per iteration; only the last was final.
# Restore: npm run render  (~90s for the 60s cut)
renders/

# Verification screenshots taken during the build.
# Restore: npx hyperframes snapshot --at <seconds>
snapshots/

# Framework caches and generated diagnostics.
.hyperframes/
.thumbnails/
.waveform-cache/
node_modules/

# Music bed. track.mp3 was retrieved from the HeyGen catalog; bed60.mp3 and
# track-ducked.mp3 are derived from it by the ffmpeg steps recorded in
# frame.md. Not deterministically reproducible — the catalog may rank a
# different track for the same query — so treat the query in BRIEF.md as the
# record, and keep a copy elsewhere if this exact bed matters.
assets/bgm/

# Narration. Regenerate from SCRIPT.md with the voice id recorded in BRIEF.md:
#   node <media-use>/audio/scripts/heygen-tts.mjs "<line>" -o assets/vo/line-N.wav \
#     --voice 0c2151d538844c70a8b096de533f2828
# Costs HeyGen allowance, so it is output rather than source.
assets/vo/

# Six cues copied from the bundled media-use SFX library. Excluded on
# licensing grounds as much as size: they are third-party audio and their
# CREDITS.md was not copied across with them.
# Restore: cp <media-use>/audio/assets/sfx/{riser,impact-bass-1,impact-bass-2,typing,click-soft,ping}.mp3 assets/sfx/
assets/sfx/
